      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{5a55a79a6765067d861f4eb4|full_name}:  I want VR chat to succeed long-term. Currently with the hosted server environment  the more users the more money it cost VR chat parent company. Some form of financial system will need to be initiated at some point in my humble opinion. Why not link it to in game activity in some way and then give the opportunity for those who don’t really want to game but do you want to make some money and support VR chat a way into the economy/metaverse that is VRChat.  If mechanical Turk can be successful. Then why not have users pay folks to do tasks in VR chat.   As the meta-verse grows that in game economy will / could eventually replace IRL income for some people This “game” has potential to become the meta-verse if it is successful long-term.  And I for one would like that to happen. As it seems that the VR chat team has their heart in the right place.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
