  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-04-04T16:09:36.263Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Raph Koster once said, \"If your virtual world is successful, your digital objects are going to have a real money value. There's no escaping it at this point...\" This quote made me think a lot about what's going to happen to VRChat and how the community's going to evolve eventually in both social and economical ways. \n\nLater, this made me realize how many worlds have things like stores, bars, vending machines, jukeboxes, arcade cabinets, tip jars, movie theaters, as well as many, many other examples. And it's just a short list of things that could be put to a good use, if only we had some sort of currency we could use in VRChat. \n\nBasically, I would suggest adding a few triggers to the VRCSDK to provide content creators with tools allowing users to earn and spend their virtual money with a support of a \"wallet\" / \"bank account\" system in order to let the players spend their \"credits\" on in-app goods and services, as well as gain virtual money by completing specific challenges, like, for example, playing or winning competitive games, including CTF, Miner Dispute, and, of course, Battle Discs, or solving specific puzzles in user-generated worlds. Obviously, in this case there needs to be some sort of limit applied to the profit players can achieve, especially in worlds created by users aside from the dev team. But it's just one of my thoughts. \n\nI'm open to other ideas regarding possibilities of this feature going live, but for now the point is pretty much the same, and it's all about adding a basic economic system to VRChat.",
